  "interpretation": [
    "Once the main directions of neutral text are removed, valence (pleasant versus unpleasant) organises the emotions (|r| = 0.85), close to Anthropic's 0.81 and Sun et al.'s 0.89.",
    "Mistakes on the independent set are human-like: angry read as afraid, anxious read as fearful, calm read as loving, desperate read as afraid, exasperated read as afraid, fearful read as desperate.",
    "The paired vectors (emotional story minus its neutral twin) share one large common direction: much of each vector is 'emotional versus flat writing'. The project therefore also tests each emotion's specific part with that common direction removed."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Held-out stories come from the same writers and format as the training stories, so high accuracy here can partly reflect vocabulary; the independent short-text set is the stronger test."
  ],
